; A decomposition names one component each, so the value is a tuple of
; exactly as many (2026-10-18, Planner.report_decomposition#): one name too
; many died in the emitter without a location, one too few or a value that is
; no tuple bound garbage at rc 0.
; xfail: a decomposition names 1 component, and the tuple has 2: (int, int)
function divmod(a: int, b: int) returns (int, int)
    (a / b, a % b)

let (a) divmod(17, 5)
print "`a`"
